---
import LandingPage from "../layouts/LandingPage.astro";
import { articleJsonLd, faqJsonLd } from "../lib/seo";
import { APP_URL } from "../lib/config";

const UPDATED = "2026-08-18";
const canonical = "/focus-room";
const title = "Online Focus Room: Quiet Timed Sessions With a Partner";
const description =
  "An online focus room is a timed, quiet session with a real person — not a 24/7 lofi lobby. Here's how virtual focus rooms work, how they differ from YouTube study-with-me, and how to join one.";

const faqs = [
  {
    question: "What is an online focus room?",
    answer:
      "An online focus room is a live, time-boxed session where you and at least one other person work on your own tasks in parallel. You share a timer, stay quiet, and use the other person's presence as gentle accountability — the same idea as a library desk, without leaving home.",
  },
  {
    question: "Is a focus room the same as a 24/7 study lobby?",
    answer:
      "No. Many apps run always-on rooms with dozens of people, ambient cafés, and open chat. A Refocus focus room is a matched 25, 50, or 75-minute session with one partner. It starts, it ends, and nobody is hanging around in a public lobby.",
  },
  {
    question: "How is a focus room different from a YouTube study-with-me video?",
    answer:
      "A recording can't tell whether you actually sat down. In a live focus room you join with a real person, set a goal, and work against a shared timer. The other person is studying or working too — not performing on a livestream.",
  },
  {
    question: "Do I need my camera on in a focus room?",
    answer:
      "Cameras stay on for presence. Mics stay quiet. You share one line about what you'll work on, then get to work — co-presence, not a meeting. You can turn your camera off anytime if you prefer.",
  },
  {
    question: "Who uses a virtual focus room?",
    answer:
      "Students grinding exam prep, remote workers who miss office energy, and anyone who focuses better around other people. If a library or café works for you but home doesn't, a focus room recreates that effect online.",
  },
];

const article = articleJsonLd({
  headline: title,
  description,
  path: canonical,
  dateModified: UPDATED,
});
---

<LandingPage
  title={title}
  description={description}
  canonical={canonical}
  eyebrow="Guide"
  heading="Online focus room: quiet sessions with a real partner"
  lead="A focus room isn't another aesthetic Pomodoro tab. It's a timed block with someone else who showed up to work — so you actually start, stay, and finish."
  updated={UPDATED}
  faqs={faqs}
  ctaTitle="Join a focus room"
  ctaText="Refocus matches you 1:1 for 25, 50, or 75 minutes. Share one line about your task, work quietly with a shared timer, and check in at the end. Free to start, no card required."
  ctaHref={`${APP_URL}/auth/sign-up`}
  ctaLabel="Start a free session"
  jsonLd={[article, faqJsonLd(faqs)]}
>
  <h2>What a focus room actually is</h2>
  <p>
    A <strong>focus room</strong> (sometimes called an online focus room or
    virtual focus room) is a live session where you work on your own task while
    someone else works on theirs. The structure is light: a one-line goal, a
    shared timer, camera on for presence, muted mics. What makes it work is the same
    thing that makes a library work — a present, focused person next to you.
    That's <a href="/body-doubling">body doubling</a>, packaged as a room you
    can join from a browser.
  </p>

  <h2>Focus room vs. always-on study lobbies</h2>
  <p>
    A lot of "focus room" products are 24/7 public spaces: lofi cafés, 100
    avatars, chat that unlocks on break. Those can feel busy. They are not what
    Refocus runs. Here a focus room is a <strong>matched session</strong> with
    one partner and a defined start and end. You are not dropping into a crowd;
    you are booking a block with someone who also came to focus.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>YouTube study-with-me</strong> is a recording. Nobody knows if
      you showed up.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Discord or a giant lobby</strong> is always on — easy to lurk,
      easy to chat.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>A Refocus focus room</strong> is 1:1, timed, and quiet. When the
      timer ends, the session ends.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>How a session runs</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Pick 25, 50, or 75 minutes.</li>
    <li>Get matched with someone who's also there to focus.</li>
    <li>Say what you'll work on in one line.</li>
    <li>Work side by side. Mics stay quiet; cameras stay on for presence.</li>
    <li>Check in at the end — what got done.</li>
  </ol>
  <p>
    Studying for an exam rather than desk work? See
    <a href="/study-with-me">study together online</a> for exam-prep rooms, or
    <a href="/study-partner">find a quiet study partner</a> if you want the
    person, not the room metaphor. Remote workers who miss office energy can
    start from <a href="/virtual-coworking">virtual coworking</a>.
  </p>
</LandingPage>
